# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# kaipu-record — code signing & notarization (macOS, Developer ID / direct download)
#
# Copy to `.env.signing` and fill in. `.env.signing` is gitignored; this .example
# is not (the `!.env.signing.example` rule keeps it tracked).
#
# These are the names electron-builder reads from the environment automatically.
# They are deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_/MAIN_VITE_, so they can never be
# inlined into the bundle.
#
# What is secret vs not:
#   - Truly secret:  the .p12 file, the .p8 file, and CSC_KEY_PASSWORD.
#   - Identifiers (not secret, already in electron-builder.yml / the signature):
#                  Team ID, Key ID, Issuer ID.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Signing (Developer ID Application) ---
# ABSOLUTE path to the .p12 (local). No spaces in the path. In CI = base64.
CSC_LINK=/Users/<user>/.secrets/kaipu/kaipu-record-signing-Certificates.p12
# Password set when EXPORTING the .p12 (not your Mac password nor your Apple ID).
CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=

# --- Notarization (App Store Connect API Key — Team Key) ---
# ABSOLUTE path to the .p8 (local). In CI = base64.
APPLE_API_KEY=/Users/<user>/.secrets/kaipu/kaipu-AuthKey_<KEY_ID>.p8
# Key ID = 10 chars (it is in the .p8 filename). For Kaipu: QWXC4HC43K
APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
# Issuer ID = UUID (App Store Connect → Users and Access → Integrations, above the table).
# Required for Team Keys. (If you ever use an Individual Key from Xcode 26+, OMIT this var.)
APPLE_API_ISSUER=
